        "id": "flask/sansio/scaffold.py::function::_find_package_path::27389",
        "kind": "function",
        "explain": "Locates the filesystem path containing the package/module named by import_name. Splits off the root module name and asks importlib.util.find_spec for it. If that raises ImportError or ValueError (invalid name, __main__, or spec None \u2014 the function raises ValueError itself when the spec is missing), it falls back to os.getcwd(). For a package (submodule_search_locations set): if origin is None or 'namespace' (namespace package), it looks up the full import_name's spec; if found with search locations, it takes the commonpath of those locations and finds the root search location that contains it (via next over an iterator, which raises StopIteration if none match); otherwise it uses the first search location; in both cases returns the parent directory (os.path.dirname). For a regular package with __init__.py, returns dirname(dirname(origin)) (two levels up from the __init__ file). For a plain module, returns dirname(origin).",
        "summary": "Resolves the filesystem directory containing a package or module.",
        "extras": [
          {
            "topic": "failure",
